## Context

Child of sweep tracker 0571. The restructure moved prose between
sections and left the same content stated 2-3 times. Reviewer findings
below (main 79d3cba3; relocate by grep — 0567/0568 will have shifted
lines). Principle: keep the structurally-primary occurrence, compress
others to a clause + \ref pointer. Do NOT delete content that does
different work in different places — compress only true repetition.

## Actions (MAJOR first)

1. ρ = 0.92 with identical gloss in §7.2 (~L858) and Conclusion
   (~L1211): keep both numbers (the Conclusion needs it) but vary the
   Conclusion to the compressed form already mandated by the brief
   (value + in-sample caveat + \ref), no re-explanation of the
   mechanism.
2. "Curated documents equalise the agents" fully developed three times
   (~L801-821 §6, ~L913-920 §7.4, ~L1205-1209 Conclusion): §6 is
   primary. In §7.4 compress the re-narration to one citing sentence
   ("Once the agents share a good document set, single-shot performance
   converges (§\ref{sec:exp2})"). Conclusion keeps its one-sentence
   version.
3. Discussion opener (~L949-956) re-narrates all three results already
   summarised in the intro (~L148-157) and §7: compress to one
   orienting sentence + the section's actual scope statement (what the
   instrument can and cannot support).
4. "Managed, auditable knowledge base ... dated snapshot" formula
   near-verbatim in §7.3 (~L899) and §7.4 (~L921): keep §7.4 (the
   system subsection); in §7.3 reduce to a forward-reference clause.
5. Intro roadmap (~L165-168) vs §7 opener (~L825-831) near-duplicate
   enumeration of the four extensions: trim the intro roadmap to "extend
   with post-hoc analyses (§\ref{sec:extensions})" without enumerating
   the four.

## Actions (MINOR — tighten if cheap)

6. Status-composition conclusion near-verbatim in §7.1 (~L843-848) and
   recognition annex (~L2361-2366): acceptable summary/full split —
   vary the annex sentence wording so it is not verbatim.
7. GPT-5.5 refusal episode told three times (~L588 §5, ~L1015
   Discussion, ~L1704 exp1 annex): §5 reports the event, Discussion
   interprets it — both stay. The annex occurrence drops the quote and
   becomes a pointer to the Discussion paragraph.
8. "Single-model ceiling" echo across §7.3/§7.4/Conclusion: functional
   echoes; reword to avoid identical phrasing, no structural change.

## Test

- Red step: none mechanical (semantic repetition is not CI-testable
  under the polarity rule). Verification is by the PR reviewer reading
  the four seams; note this explicitly in the PR body.

